text:
Alex: Quick heads up — the new sample for ESM + edge runtime is failing typechecks and also shows weird auth/retry behavior when built as NodeNext.

Maria: Can you paste the repro? minimal steps?

Alex: Repro (very condensed):

```ts
// sdk/index.ts
export function createClient(key: string): Client;
export function createClient(opts: { key?: string; retry?: number }): Client;
export function createClient(arg: any) {
  // runtime handles both
}
```

and package.json exports:

```json
{
  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "import": "./dist/esm/index.js",
      "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js"
    }
  }
}
```

When built for NodeNext the compiler loses generic inference around overloads and our sample app gets lots of `any`. Also the edge build (Vite/Rollup) ends up bundling the CJS types or dropping the types entry, so the editor shows `any` for client methods.

Joel: Sounds like two separate issues: runtime (edge vs node fetch/AbortController) and types resolution. For types, try `module: "NodeNext"` + `moduleResolution: "Bundler"` or `"NodeNext"` in the sample tsconfig, and add `types`/`typesVersions` in package.json so TS knows where to look for ESM vs CJS typings.

CI Bot: Build log snippet:
```
src/app.ts:15:12 - error TS2322: Type 'unknown' is not assignable to type 'string'.
```

Sam: The auth/retry break is because edge runtime's fetch doesn't include `signal` semantics the same way in our adapter; aborts aren't propagated, so retry abort logic never fires and we leak retries. Quick hack for samples: polyfill global fetch/AbortController in the edge dev bundle.

Maria: For typings we should avoid relying on overloads that return the same runtime type — switch to a single generic signature with constrained generics, e.g.

```ts
export function createClient<T extends ClientOptions = ClientOptions>(opts?: T): ClientFor<T>;
```

That avoids ambiguous overload inference when TS resolves different module modes.

Alex: So do we change the SDK, the sample tsconfig, or both?

Joel: Opening a PR to upstream the typing change + add separate "types/esm" build and a `typesVersions` mapping. I'll also add a README note about `moduleResolution` for sample apps. PR -> https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/4821 :tada:

Maria: For the edge auth flaky bit, create a small wrapper in the sample that injects a fetch shim and test in the edge preview. We should also make the SDK defensive (check for missing `signal` and fallback to timeout-based aborts).

Alex: Awesome — thanks everyone. I'll update the sample app once Joel's PR merges. :+1:
